---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Methodology - Slovak Brain Drain" lang="en">
  <h1>Methodology and Sources</h1>
  <p>Full data provenance, source quality ratings, and known limitations.</p>

  <section class="methodology-content">
    <h2>Data sources</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Source</th><th>Coverage</th><th>Confidence</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>SU SR DataCube</td><td>11 cubes, 2004-2025</td><td>Very high</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Eurostat</td><td>8 datasets</td><td>High</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Census 2021</td><td>9 indicators, 2,927 obec</td><td>Very high</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Census 2011</td><td>Education at okres level</td><td>High</td></tr>
        <tr><td>OECD</td><td>5 migration datasets</td><td>Medium-high</td></tr>
        <tr><td>CSU (Czech)</td><td>4 tables, 2004-2025</td><td>High</td></tr>
        <tr><td>UN DESA</td><td>Bilateral stock, 1990-2020</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Known discrepancies</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>CSU reports ~12% more Slovaks in CZ than OECD/DESA (different counting methods: residence permits vs census-based "born in Slovakia")</li>
      <li>2011 Census correction creates a discontinuity in population time series</li>
      <li>OECD uses ISO3 country codes, UN DESA uses numeric codes</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Validation report</h2>
    <p>5 cross-source checks run. 0 red flags, 4 yellow flags (documented discrepancies). Full report available in the repository.</p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .methodology-content { max-width: 780px; }
  .methodology-content h2 { font-family: var(--font-heading); margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  th, td { padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5; }
  th { font-weight: 600; background: #f8f9fa; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
</style>
